<title>USA: Capital Bancorp Q3 net rises, shr falls.</title>
<headline>Capital Bancorp Q3 net rises, shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>CAPITAL BANCORP AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>SUMMARY OF CONSOLIDATED THIRD QUARTER EARNINGS</p>
<p>	    PERIOD ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 1996</p>
<p>			  (Unaudited)</p>
<p>		(In thousands except for per share data)</p>
<p>RESULTS 0F OPERATIONS,</p>
<p>   for the quarter ended September 30:    1996	    1995</p>
<p> Net interest income			 $16,733	  $18,111</p>
<p> Provisions for credit losses		1,575	    2,400</p>
<p> Non-interest income			  13,627	   12,352</p>
<p> Non-interest expense			 19,782(1)	19,931</p>
<p> Net income					5,119	    5,024</p>
<p> Earnings per share			     0.64	     0.66</p>
<p> Return on assets(2)			  1.19 %	   1.36 %</p>
<p> Return on equity(2)			 16.15 %	  19.01 %</p>
<p> Net interest margin(3)		     5.32 %	   5.73 %</p>
<p>RESULTS OF OPERATIONS,</p>
<p>for the nine months ended September 30:</p>
<p> Net interest income			  50,717	   50,441</p>
<p> Provisions for credit losses		5,975	    4,100</p>
<p> Non-interest income			  38,858	   34,369</p>
<p> Non-interest expense			 58,914(1)	60,325</p>
<p> Net income				     14,686	   12,685</p>
<p> Earnings per share			     1.81	     1.67</p>
<p> Return on assets(2)			  1.21 %	   1.22 %</p>
<p> Return on equity(2)			 16.31 %	  17.05 %</p>
<p> Net interest margin(3)		     5.33 %	   5.96 %</p>
<p>(1)  Includes $513,000 of minority interest in consolidated subsidiary.</p>
<p>(2)  Annualized</p>
<p>(3)  Annualized, tax equivalent</p>
<p>(4)  1995 capital ratios have been restated to conform with 1996</p>
<p>	   calculations. SOURCE  Capital Bancorp</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
